  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1927; the four retiring councillors were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1927, p. 8). 'Mr. J. W. Fleming ... sat in nominations for the Cookstown ... vacancies created by the retirement of the four councillors on the urban council. These — Messrs. D. H. Hamilton, G. Ferguson, J. M'D. Scott, and Samuel M'Kinney — were returned, and there will, therefore, be no [election].' Returned unopposed."
